main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ parenthesized: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.new]/24, [dcl.init.general]/16.5 (P0960): `new int[3](1, 2)'
initializes the elements from the parenthesized expression-list as from
a braced list: 1, 2, 0.  The front end reports "new with array type and
parenthesized initializer is not supported" (bin53 crashed on it).
cpp11_array_new_value_and_list_initialization covers the braced form.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
